[{"text":"client.collect().await","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":247,"end":269},"start":{"line":6,"column":18},"end":{"line":6,"column":40}},"file":"skill_improvement/evidence/queries/non_datafusion_collect.rs","lines":"    let _events = client.collect().await;","charCount":{"leading":18,"trailing":1},"language":"Rust","metaVariables":{"single":{},"multi":{"secondary":[{"text":"collect","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":254,"end":261},"start":{"line":6,"column":25},"end":{"line":6,"column":32}}},{"text":"client.collect","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":247,"end":261},"start":{"line":6,"column":18},"end":{"line":6,"column":32}}},{"text":"client.collect()","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":247,"end":263},"start":{"line":6,"column":18},"end":{"line":6,"column":34}}}]},"transformed":{}},"ruleId":"project-collect-over-stream","severity":"hint","note":"`collect()` materializes every RecordBatch before returning. `execute_stream()` and\n`execute_stream_partitioned()` yield batches as they are produced, which bounds memory and lets\na caller stop early. Collecting is correct for small results and for tests -- this is a prompt\nto check, not a defect.\n\nAnchored to an awaited call, because DataFusion's `collect` is async and `Iterator::collect`\nis not. Without that anchor this rule matches every iterator in the repository: 298 hits\ninstead of the handful that concern DataFusion.\n","message":"Whole result collected into memory; a streaming execution path exists.","labels":[{"text":"client.collect().await","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":247,"end":269},"start":{"line":6,"column":18},"end":{"line":6,"column":40}},"style":"primary"},{"text":"collect","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":254,"end":261},"start":{"line":6,"column":25},"end":{"line":6,"column":32}},"style":"secondary"},{"text":"client.collect","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":247,"end":261},"start":{"line":6,"column":18},"end":{"line":6,"column":32}},"style":"secondary"},{"text":"client.collect()","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":